{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["If the thief is not found, and he is brought near, etc. — Our Sages interpreted: אם לא ימצא, as the bailee said: it was stolen from me, but he himself stole it, and if he is brought near and swears before the judges, he pays double when the judges convict him and pays twofold to the other party. But I shall interpret it according to the plain sense: if the thief is not found and the master of the house — that is, the bailee — is brought near, that he did not lay his hand against his fellow's property — rather, it was stolen from him, and he goes exempt."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:33.577847339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}